  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1014 PM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nWe will finally see a break in cloudy skies on Wednesday. The \nstratus layer is expected to prevail through Wednesday morning \nbefore gradually burning off through the afternoon hours. With \nsunshine finally returning, we will see a warm up in temperatures, \nalthough only by a few degrees as the clouds will be slow to clear. \nThe rest of the week is expected to be quiet and mild with highs in \nthe 60s everyday. Previous forecasts had precipitation chances later \nin the week. Models indicated the shortwave that was mentioned in \nthe short term discussion would clip our region possibly bring \nshowers. However, current model runs have the shortwave passing well \nnorth of the forecast area. Therefore, precipitation chances have \ndropped to near zero for Thursday and Friday. We are still a few \ndays away and models will certainly change, however we could see a \ncold front this weekend that could bring cooler temperatures and \nprecipitation chances to the start of next week.",
